# pulse starter: hello ({{.Lang}})

One function behind `GET /hello`. The smallest possible pulse app —
no queues, no tables, no schema: `resources` is only ever needed for what
you actually use.

```bash
pulse start
curl "localhost:3000/hello?name=you"
```

Then make it yours: edit {{if eq .Lang "python"}}`functions/hello/handler.py`{{else}}`functions/hello/index.mjs`{{end}} and save — the next
request runs the new code, no restart. `pulse logs hello -f` streams what
it prints.

Grow it with one command at a time:

```bash
pulse add function <name>                 # another function
pulse add route POST /things --function <name>
pulse add queue jobs --worker <name>      # background jobs
pulse add table things --pk id            # persistence
```

Prefer the other language? `pulse init <name> --template hello --lang node|python`
